{"subjectId":"dsa-advanced","id":"sorting","title":"Sorting","group":"","order":6,"html":"<h4>Overview of sorting Algorithm</h4>\n<p>1. Binary Array</p>\n<p>2. Array of three values</p>\n<p>3. Array of Size n and Small ranged value</p>\n<p>4. Array of size n and range is of size n^2 or n^3 or closer</p>\n<p>5. Array of uniformly distributed data over a range</p>\n<p>6. When memory writes are costly</p>\n<p>7. When adjacent swaps are allowed</p>\n<p>8. When array size is small</p>\n<p>9. When available extra memory is less</p>\n<h4>General Purpose Sorting Algorithm</h4>\n<p>-&gt; Merge Sort</p>\n<p>-&gt; Heap Sort</p>\n<p>-&gt; Quick Sort</p>\n<h4>Hybrid Algorithm (Used in Algorithm)</h4>\n<p>-&gt; Tim Sort</p>\n<p>-&gt; Intro Sort</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3>Tail call Elimination in Quick Sort</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def partition(arr, l, r):\n    pivot = arr[r]\n    i = l - 1\n\n    for j in range(l, r):\n        if arr[j] &lt;= pivot:\n            i += 1\n            arr[i], arr[j] = arr[j], arr[i]\n    arr[i + 1], arr[r] = arr[r], arr[i + 1]\n\n    return i + 1\n\ndef qsort(arr, l, r):\n  if l &lt; r:\n    p = partition(arr, l, r)\n    qsort(arr, l, p)\n    qsort(arr, p+1, r)\n\n# NOTE : No expectation or No returns for the last recursive call that is called as Tail Call function\n\n# Tail Call Optimization\n\ndef qsort(arr, l, r):\n  while l &lt; r:\n    p = partition(arr, l, r)\n    qsort(arr, l, p)\n    l = p + 1</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Kth Smallest Element</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> [10, 5, 30, 12] ; k = 2<br><strong>Output:</strong> 10</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef kthsmall(arr, k):\n  arr.sort()\n  return arr[k-1]\n\narr = [10, 5, 30, 12]\nkthsmall(arr, 2)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef lomutoPartition(arr, l, r):\n    pivot = arr[r]\n    i = l - 1\n\n    for j in range(l, r):\n        if arr[j] &lt;= pivot:\n            i += 1\n            arr[i], arr[j] = arr[j], arr[i]\n\n    arr[i + 1], arr[r] = arr[r], arr[i + 1]\n    return i + 1\n\ndef kthsmall(arr, k):\n  l = 0\n  r = len(arr) - 1\n\n  while l &lt;= r:\n    p = lomutoPartition(arr, l, r)\n\n    if p == k - 1:\n      return arr[p]\n\n    elif p &gt; k - 1:\n      r = p - 1\n\n    else:\n      l = p + 1\n\n  return -1\n\narr = [10, 5, 30, 12]\nkthsmall(arr, 2)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Minimum Difference in an Array</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [1, 8, 12, 5, 18]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 3<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [8, 15]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 7<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [10]<br><strong>Output:</strong> INF</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef minDiff(arr):\n  res = float(\"inf\")\n\n  for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n    for j in range(i):\n      res = min(res, abs(arr[i] - arr[j]))\n\n  return res\n\narr = [1, 8, 12, 5, 18]\nminDiff(arr)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n'''\n-&gt; Sort the Array\n-&gt; Compute Difference between adjacent elements\n-&gt; Return the minimum of values found in step 2\n'''\n\ndef minDiff(arr):\n  res = float(\"inf\")\n  arr.sort()\n\n  for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n    res = min(res, abs(arr[i] - arr[i - 1]))\n\n  return res\n\narr = [1, 8, 12, 5, 18]\nminDiff(arr)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Chocolate Distribution Problem</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [7, 3, 2, 4, 9, 12, 56] ; m = 3<br><strong>Output:</strong> 2<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [3, 4, 1, 9, 56, 7, 9, 12] ; m = 5<br><strong>Output:</strong> 6</p>\n</div>\n<p>Idea for the Solution</p>\n<p>1. Consider every item as minimum one by one</p>\n<p>2. minimum of all the values is 2</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def minDiff(arr, m):\n  if m == 0 or len(arr) == 0:\n    return 0\n\n  if len(arr) &lt; m:\n    return -1\n\n  arr.sort()\n  res = arr[m-1] - arr[0]\n\n  for i in range(1, len(arr) - m + 1):\n    res = min(res, arr[i+m-1] - arr[i])\n\n  return res\n\narr = [1, 8, 12, 5, 18]\nm = 3\nminDiff(arr, 3)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Sort an Array with Two Types</h3>\n<p>-&gt; Segregate Positive and Negative</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [15, 18, -3, -2]<br><strong>Output:</strong> [-3, -2, 15, 18]</p>\n</div>\n<p>-&gt; Segregate Even and Odd</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] [15, 14, 13, 12]<br><strong>Output:</strong> [14, 12, 15, 13]</p>\n</div>\n<p>-&gt; Sort an Binary Array</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [0, 1, 1, 1, 0]<br><strong>Output:</strong> [0, 0, 1, 1, 1]</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def segregatePosNeg(arr):\n    j = 0\n\n    for i in range(len(arr)):\n        if arr[i] &lt; 0:\n            arr[i], arr[j] = arr[j], arr[i]\n            j += 1\n\n    return arr\n\narr = [15, 18, -3, -2]\nprint(segregatePosNeg(arr))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def segregateEvenOdd(arr):\n    j = 0\n\n    for i in range(len(arr)):\n        if arr[i] % 2 == 0:\n            arr[i], arr[j] = arr[j], arr[i]\n            j += 1\n\n    return arr\n\narr = [15, 14, 13, 12]\nprint(segregateEvenOdd(arr))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def sortBinaryArray(arr):\n    j = 0\n\n    for i in range(len(arr)):\n        if arr[i] == 0:\n            arr[i], arr[j] = arr[j], arr[i]\n            j += 1\n\n    return arr\n\narr = [0, 1, 1, 1, 0]\nprint(sortBinaryArray(arr))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef sorts(arr):\n  n = len(arr)\n  temp = [0] * n\n  i = 0\n\n  for j in range(0, n):\n    if arr[j] == 0:\n      temp[i] = arr[j]\n      i += 1\n\n  for j in range(0, n):\n    if arr[j] == 1:\n      temp[i] = arr[j]\n      i += 1\n\n  print(temp)\n\narr = [0, 1, 1, 1, 0]\nsorts(arr)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef sorts(arr):\n    i, j = 0, len(arr) - 1\n\n    while i &lt; j:\n\n        while i &lt; j and arr[i] == 0:\n            i += 1\n\n        while i &lt; j and arr[j] == 1:\n            j -= 1\n\n        if i &lt; j:\n            arr[i], arr[j] = arr[j], arr[i]\n            i += 1\n            j -= 1\n\narr = [0, 1, 1, 1, 0]\nsorts(arr)\nprint(arr)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Sort an Array with Three Types</h3>\n<p>-&gt; Sort an Array of 0s, 1s, 2s</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [0, 1, 2, 1, 1, 2]<br><strong>Output:</strong> [0, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2]</p>\n</div>\n<p>-&gt; Three way Partitioning</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> [2, 1, 2, 20, 10, 20, 1] ; pivot = 2<br><strong>Output:</strong> [1, 1, 2, 2, 20, 10, 20]</p>\n</div>\n<p>-&gt; Partition Around a Range</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> [10, 5, 6, 3, 20, 9, 40] ; range = [5, 10]<br><strong>Output:</strong> [3, 5, 6, 9, 10, 20, 40]</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef sortArr(arr):\n  temp = []\n\n  for x in arr:\n    if x == 0:\n      temp.append(x)\n\n  for x in arr:\n    if x == 1:\n      temp.append(x)\n\n  for x in arr:\n    if x == 2:\n      temp.append(x)\n\n  return temp\n\narr = [0, 1, 2, 1, 1, 2]\nprint(sortArr(arr))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution : Dutch National Flag Algorithm\n\ndef sort012(arr):\n    low, mid, high = 0, 0, len(arr) - 1\n\n    while mid &lt;= high:\n\n        if arr[mid] == 0:\n            arr[low], arr[mid] = arr[mid], arr[low]\n            low += 1\n            mid += 1\n\n        elif arr[mid] == 1:\n            mid += 1\n\n        else:\n            arr[high], arr[mid] = arr[mid], arr[high]\n            high -= 1\n\n    return arr\n\narr = [0, 1, 2, 1, 1, 2]\nprint(sort012(arr))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def threeWayPartition(arr, pivot):\n    low, mid, high = 0, 0, len(arr) - 1\n\n    while mid &lt;= high:\n        if arr[mid] &lt; pivot:\n            arr[low], arr[mid] = arr[mid], arr[low]\n            low += 1\n            mid += 1\n        elif arr[mid] == pivot:\n            mid += 1\n        else:\n            arr[high], arr[mid] = arr[mid], arr[high]\n            high -= 1\n\n    return arr\n\narr = [2, 1, 2, 20, 10, 20, 1]\npivot = 2\nprint(threeWayPartition(arr, pivot))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def partitionAroundRange(arr, L, U):\n    less = [x for x in arr if x &lt; L]\n    middle = [x for x in arr if L &lt;= x &lt;= U]\n    greater = [x for x in arr if x &gt; U]\n\n    return less + middle + greater\n\narr = [1, 2, 10, 5, 6, 3, 20, 9, 40]\nL, U = 5, 10\nprint(partitionAroundRange(arr, L, U))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Merge Overlapping intervals</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> [ [1, 3], [2, 4], [5, 7], [6, 8] ]<br><strong>Output:</strong> [ [1, 4], [5, 8] ]<br><strong>Input:</strong> [ [7, 9], [6, 10], [4, 5], [1, 3], [2, 4] ]<br><strong>Output:</strong> [ [1, 5], [6, 10] ]</p>\n</div>\n<h4>How to check if Two Intervals Overlap...?</h4>\n<h4>Naive</h4>\n<p>For every interval x, do:</p>\n<p>1. Check if x overlap with other intervals</p>\n<ul>\n<li>In case of merge</li>\n</ul>\n<p> 1. Update x</p>\n<p> 2. Delete the Other Interval</p>\n<p>Time : O(n^3)</p>\n<h4>Efficient Solution</h4>\n<p>1. Sort by start Time, Let the sorted array be: x0, x1,.... xi-1, xi, ..... xn-1</p>\n<p>2. Let us assume that we have merged till xi [j &lt; i] : m0, m1,..... mj-1, mj</p>\n<p>Claim: xi cannot merge with m0, m1,.... mj-1</p>\n<p>Proof :</p>\n<p>-&gt; xi.start &gt;= mj.start</p>\n<p>-&gt; mj-1.end &lt; mj.start</p>\n<p>From the Above two</p>\n<p>-&gt; xi.start &gt; mj-1.end</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef mergeIntervals(arr):\n  arr.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n  res = 0\n\n  for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n    if arr[res][1] &gt;= arr[i][0]:\n      arr[res][1] = max(arr[res][1], arr[i][1])\n    else:\n      res = res + 1\n      arr[res] = arr[i]\n\n  for i in range(res + 1):\n    print(arr[i], end = \" \")\n\narr = [[1, 3], [2, 4], [5, 7], [6, 8]]\nmergeIntervals(arr)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Meeting Maximum Guests</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [900, 940] ; dep[] = [1000, 1030]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 2<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [800, 700, 600, 500] ; dep[] = [840, 820, 830, 530]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 3</p>\n</div>\n<p>Condition : 000 &lt;= arr[i], dep[] &lt;= 2359</p>\n<h4>Idea for Efficient Solution</h4>\n<p>Consider all Events in sorted order &amp; count Guests</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def maxGuests(arr, dep):\n  arr.sort()\n  dep.sort()\n\n  n = len(arr)\n  i, j = 1, 0\n  curr, res = 1, 0\n\n  while i &lt; n and j &lt; n:\n    if arr[i] &lt;= dep[j]:\n      curr += 1\n      i += 1\n\n    else:\n      curr -= 1\n      j += 1\n\n    res = max(res, curr)\n\n  return res\n\narr = [800, 700, 600, 500]\ndep = [840, 820, 830, 530]\nprint(maxGuests(arr, dep))\n\narr = []\ndep = []\nprint(maxGuests(arr, dep))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Counting Sort</h3>\n<p>A θ(n+k) algorithm to sort elements in range from 0 to k-1</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [1, 4, 4, 1, 0, 1] ; k = 5<br><strong>Output:</strong> arr[] = [0, 1, 1, 1, 4, 4]</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def Countingsort(arr, k):\n  count = [0] * k\n\n  for x in arr:\n    count[x] += 1\n\n  index = 0\n\n  for i in range(k):\n    for j in range(count[i]):\n      arr[index] = i\n      index += 1\n\narr = [1, 4, 4, 1, 0, 1]\nk = 5\nCountingsort(arr, k)\nprint(arr)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>'''\n# Problem with previous Implementation\n\n-&gt; Would not work for an array of objects like an array of students to be sorted by marks\n\n# Important Points\n\n-&gt; Not a comparison based Algorithm\n-&gt; Time Complexity : θ(n + k)\n-&gt; Space Complexity : θ(n + k)\n-&gt; Stable\n-&gt; used as a sub routine in radix sort\n'''\n\n# Updated Solution\n\ndef countingSort(arr, k):\n  output = [0] * len(arr)\n  count = [0] * k\n\n  for x in arr:\n    count[x] += 1\n\n  for i in range(1, k):\n    count[i] += count[i-1]\n\n  for x in reversed(arr):\n    output[count[x] - 1] = x\n    count[x] -= 1\n\n  for i in range(len(arr)):\n    arr[i] = output[i]\n\narr = [1, 4, 4, 1, 0, 1]\nk = 5\nCountingsort(arr, k)\nprint(arr)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Extend the given implementation to work for arbitrary range of size K\n\ndef countingSort(arr):\n    min_val = min(arr)\n    max_val = max(arr)\n\n    range_of_elements = max_val - min_val + 1\n\n    count = [0] * range_of_elements\n    output = [0] * len(arr)\n\n    for x in arr:\n        count[x - min_val] += 1\n\n    for i in range(1, len(count)):\n        count[i] += count[i - 1]\n\n    for x in reversed(arr):\n        output[count[x - min_val] - 1] = x\n        count[x - min_val] -= 1\n\n    for i in range(len(arr)):\n        arr[i] = output[i]\n\narr = [1, -2, 4, 4, -1, 1, 0]\ncountingSort(arr)\nprint(arr)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Cycle Sort</h3>\n<p>1. A Worst case O(n^2)</p>\n<p>2. Does minimum memory writes and can be useful for cases where memory writes is costly</p>\n<p>3. In-place and Not-stable</p>\n<p>4. Useful to Solve questions like find minimum swaps required to sort an array</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def cycleSort(arr):\n    for cs in range(len(arr) - 1):\n        item = arr[cs]\n        pos = cs\n\n        for i in range(cs + 1, len(arr)):\n            if arr[i] &lt; item:\n                pos += 1\n\n        if pos == cs:\n            continue\n\n        while item == arr[pos]: # For duplicates\n            pos += 1\n\n        arr[pos], item = item, arr[pos]\n\n        while pos != cs:\n            pos = cs\n\n            for i in range(cs + 1, len(arr)):\n                if arr[i] &lt; item:\n                    pos += 1\n\n            while item == arr[pos]:\n                pos += 1\n\n            arr[pos], item = item, arr[pos]\n\narr = [30, 40, 50, 10, 20, 50]\ncycleSort(arr)\nprint(arr)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Radix Sort</h3>\n<p>319, 212, 6, 8, 100, 50</p>\n<p>-&gt; Re-writing numbers with leading Zeros</p>\n<p>319, 212, 006, 008, 100, 050</p>\n<p>-&gt; Stable Sort according the last digit (Least Significant Digit)</p>\n<p>100, 050, 212, 006, 008, 319</p>\n<p>-&gt; Stable Sort according to the middle Digit</p>\n<p>100, 006, 008, 212, 319, 050</p>\n<p>-&gt; Stable Sort accorging to most significant Digit</p>\n<p>006, 008, 050, 100, 212, 319</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def countingSort(arr, exp):\n  output = [0] * len(arr)\n  count = [0] * 10\n\n  for i in range(0, len(arr)):\n    index = (arr[i]//exp) % 10\n    count[index] += 1\n\n  for i in range(1, 10):\n    count[i] += count[i-1]\n\n  i = len(arr) - 1\n\n  while i &gt;= 0:\n    index = (arr[i]//exp) % 10\n    output[count[index]-1] = arr[i]\n    count[index] -= 1\n    i -= 1\n\n  for i in range(0, len(arr)):\n    arr[i] = output[i]\n\ndef radixSort(arr):\n  mx = max(arr)\n  exp = 1\n\n  while mx/exp &gt; 1:\n    countingSort(arr, exp)\n    exp *= 10\n\narr = [319, 212, 6, 8, 100, 50 ]\nradixSort(arr)\nprint(arr)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Bucket Sort</h3>\n<p>-&gt; Consider a Situation where we have numbers uniformly distributed in range from 1 to 10^8</p>\n<p>-&gt; Consider another situation where we have floating point numbers uniformly distrbuted in range from 0.0 to 1.0</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> 20, 88, 70, 85, 75, 95, 18, 82, 60 ; Range 0 to 99</p>\n</div>\n<p>Step 1 : Scatter</p>\n<p>-&gt; 00 - 19 : 18</p>\n<p>-&gt; 20 - 39 : 20</p>\n<p>-&gt; 40 - 59 :</p>\n<p>-&gt; 60 - 79 : 70, 75, 60</p>\n<p>-&gt; 80 - 99 : 88, 85, 95, 92</p>\n<p>Step 2 : Sort Buckets</p>\n<p>-&gt; 00 - 19 : 18</p>\n<p>-&gt; 20 - 39 : 20</p>\n<p>-&gt; 40 - 59 :</p>\n<p>-&gt; 60 - 79 : 60, 70, 75</p>\n<p>-&gt; 80 - 99 : 85, 88, 92, 95</p>\n<p>Step 3 : Join Sorted Buckets</p>\n<p>-&gt; 18, 20, 60, 70, 75, 85, 88, 92, 95</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def bucketSort(arr, k):\n  rs = max(arr) + 1\n\n  bkt = [[] for i in range(k)]\n\n  for x in arr:\n    i = (k*x)//rs\n    bkt[i].append(x)\n\n  for i in range(k):\n    bkt[i].sort()\n\n  idx = 0\n\n  for i in range(k):\n    for j in range(len(bkt[i])):\n      arr[idx] = bkt[i][j]\n      idx += 1\n\narr = [20, 88, 70, 85, 75, 95, 18, 82, 60]\nk = 20\nbucketSort(arr, k)\nprint(arr)</code></pre></figure></section>"}